From: bakhodirovxz <bohodirovasadbek1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:50:44 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 18/22] xlsx, engine: read an XLSX file from the file, not from
 its bytes

Opening held the whole file in memory while the workbook was built:
79 MB for an 80 MB workbook, 160 MB for a 120 MB one saved by Excel, at
the time opening needs the most memory once the recalculation on open
is smaller (or skipped).

`Package` now reads its parts from any `Read + Seek` source
(`read_xlsx_reader`); `read_xlsx` reads from the bytes as before. When
file.open's bytes sniff as XLSX, it frees them and reads the package from
the file (`io::open_xlsx_file`), checking that the file still has the
size it had. Other formats, base64 input and encrypted workbooks are read
from their bytes as before.
